cabulary"},{"level":"B1","questions":8,"focus":"Present perfect vs past simple, future forms, first conditional, modals, B1 vocabulary"},{"level":"B1+","questions":6,"focus":"Past perfect, passive, second conditional, relative clauses, collocations"},{"level":"B2","questions":4,"focus":"Reported speech, third conditional, modals of deduction, B2 vocabulary"}],"bands":[{"band":"A2","description":"''Getting there'' on most criteria: short, simple sentences; frequent errors that sometimes block meaning."},{"band":"B1","description":"''On target'' on most criteria: the task is done clearly; errors do not block meaning."},{"band":"B1+","description":"''Beyond target'' on most criteria: some range and longer, linked sentences."},{"band":"B2","description":"''Beyond target'' on all criteria: wide range, accurate complex sentences, well organised."}],"decisionRules":[{"outcome":"Foundation course","testScore":"0–11","samples":"Or both samples at A2, whatever the test score."},{"outcome":"Stage 1","testScore":"12–18","samples":"At least one sample at B1 or above."},{"outcome":"Stage 2","testScore":"19–24","samples":"Both samples at B1+ or above."}],"borderline":"If the score is within one point of a boundary, or the test and samples point to different results, place the learner in the lower option and tell them they can take a short move-up check after week 2. Where a teacher is involved, they review borderline cases first.","learnerChoice":"A learner placed in Stage 2 may choose to start at Stage 1. A learner placed in the foundation course is shown why, with links to suitable A2 material.","efSetCrossCheck":"If the EF SET result differs from the placement by a full CEFR level or more, the placement is flagged for review; it is not changed automatically."},"checkpoint1":{"intro":"A course checkpoint, not a CEFR placement or certification test. It assesses B1 grammar, a short spoken narrative and a 150-word piece, and is reported beside the learner''s EF SET starting test.",