  ('checkpoint-1', 'Checkpoint 1', '{"version":"2026-11-21","note":"Cut scores and thresholds are provisional until the pilot calibrates them.","writingDescriptors":{"intro":"Writing is marked on the same four criteria as speaking, with B1 as the target for weeks 1–4. Learners see ''Getting there'', ''On target'' or ''Beyond target'' for each criterion, never a number.","criteria":[{"key":"task_achievement","label":"Task achievement","gettingThere":"Misses one or more required points, or under 100 words; the reader would be unsure of the purpose.","onTarget":"Covers every required point in 120–150 words; the text suits its reader (a friend, a flatmate, a visitor).","beyondTarget":"Develops every point with detail, reasons or examples, with a clear sense of the reader."},{"key":"vocabulary","label":"Vocabulary","gettingThere":"Basic, repeated words; errors with common words sometimes block meaning.","onTarget":"Enough everyday vocabulary for the topic; at least two of the week''s featured items used correctly; spelling mostly correct.","beyondTarget":"A wider range, accurate collocations, few spelling errors, and paraphrase where a word is missing."},{"key":"grammar","label":"Grammar","gettingThere":"Frequent errors in the week''s main form; some sentences are hard to follow.","onTarget":"The week''s main form used correctly at least once; simple sentences mostly accurate; errors do not block meaning.","beyondTarget":"Main and light forms used accurately; some longer sentences (relative clauses, time clauses, linkers)."},{"key":"organisation","label":"Organisation","gettingThere":"No clear order or paragraphs; few or no linkers.","onTarget":"A clear beginning, middle and end; paragraphs or clear sections; basic linkers, including the week''s linkers.","beyondTarget":"Well-built paragraphs, varied linkers, and a clear opening and closing."}],"rules":["Length. Under 100 words caps task achievement at ''Getting there''. Over 180 words is not penalised, but feedback suggests cutting.","Spelling. British spelling is taught; American spelling is noted once but not marked as an error.","Honesty. Pasted text, or a sudden jump well above the learner''s usual writing, is flagged for teacher review where a teacher is involved. Checkpoint writing has pasting disabled.","Spanish-speaker errors. Typical Spanish-speaker errors (missing subjects, false friends) are corrected like any other error and logged, so later Spanish-specific notes can draw on them."],"learnerFeedback":"A band for each criterion; one strength quoting the learner''s words; up to two corrections, prioritising the week''s grammar, each with the corrected sentence; then revise-and-retry with a word-by-word comparison of the two drafts.","wordRanges":[{"weeks":"1-4","range":"120–150 words","targetBand":"B1"},{"weeks":"5-8","range":"150–180 words","targetBand":"B1"},{"weeks":"9-12","range":"180–200 words","targetBand":"B1+"},{"weeks":"13-16","range":"200–220 words","targetBand":"B1+"},{"weeks":"Stage 2","range":"220–260 words","targetBand":"B2"}]},"placement":{"durationMinutes":35,"intro":"Placement takes about 35 minutes at sign-up and sends each learner to the foundation course, Stage 1 or Stage 2. The EF SET starting test is taken alongside it as the progress baseline, but placement makes the decision.","parts":[{"part":"Placement test","time":"15 min","what":"24 questions: 10 grammar, 6 vocabulary, 4 reading (one short text), 4 listening (two short clips)","markedBy":"App"},{"part":"Speaking sample","time":"3 min","what":"''Tell me about your job or studies, and what you''d like to be doing in two years'' time.'' 60 seconds, 30 seconds to plan.","markedBy":"AI, on the placement scale"},{"part":"Writing sample","time":"15 min","what":"''Write 80–100 words about a recent trip or event: what happened and what you enjoyed most.''","markedBy":"AI, on the placement scale"}],"questionBlueprint":[{"level":"A2","questions":6,"focus":"Past simple, comparatives, can / have to, everyday vocabulary"},{"level":"B1","questions":8,"focus":"Present perfect vs past simple, future forms, first conditional, modals, B1 vocabulary"},{"level":"B1+","questions":6,"focus":"Past perfect, passive, second conditional, relative clauses, collocations"},{"level":"B2","questions":4,"focus":"Reported speech, third conditional, modals of deduction, B2 vocabulary"}],"bands":[{"band":"A2","description":"''Getting there'' on most criteria: short, simple sentences; frequent errors that sometimes block meaning."},{"band":"B1","description":"''On target'' on most criteria: the task is done clearly; errors do not block meaning."},{"band":"B1+","description":"''Beyond target'' on most criteria: some range and longer, linked sentences."},{"band":"B2","description":"''Beyond target'' on all criteria: wide range, accurate complex sentences, well organised."}],"decisionRules":[{"outcome":"Foundation course","testScore":"0–11","samples":"Or both samples at A2, whatever the test score."},{"outcome":"Stage 1","testScore":"12–18","samples":"At least one sample at B1 or above."},{"outcome":"Stage 2","testScore":"19–24","samples":"Both samples at B1+ or above."}],"borderline":"If the score is within one point of a boundary, or the test and samples point to different results, place the learner in the lower option and tell them they can take a short move-up check after week 2. Where a teacher is involved, they review borderline cases first.","learnerChoice":"A learner placed in Stage 2 may choose to start at Stage 1. A learner placed in the foundation course is shown why, with links to suitable A2 material.","efSetCrossCheck":"If the EF SET result differs from the placement by a full CEFR level or more, the placement is flagged for review; it is not changed automatically."},"checkpoint1":{"intro":"A course checkpoint, not a CEFR placement or certification test. It assesses B1 grammar, a short spoken narrative and a 150-word piece, and is reported beside the learner''s EF SET starting test.","quiz":{"scoredItems":20,"reserveItems":4,"blueprint":"Four Main items and one Light item per week, written separately from the practice item bank so the checkpoint tests learning, not memory of practice items. Order: weeks 1–4, Main then Light. Exclude stretch tasks.","delivery":"Each item is auto-marked; the reason is shown only after the whole checkpoint is submitted. Short scenarios and answer keys allow valid variants; if two options are grammatical, ask which better expresses the stated meaning or accept both.","reporting":"Report results by skill and recommend a specific practice item."},"items":[{"id":"CP1-01","week":1,"target":"Main: finished time","prompt":"We ___ the Colosseum when we were in Rome in 2019.","options":["visited","have visited"],"key":"visited","reason":"''In 2019'' is a finished time."},{"id":"CP1-02","week":1,"target":"Main: past to now","prompt":"My brother ___ three different jobs since he left university.","options":["had","has had"],"key":"has had","reason":"''Since he left'' connects the past to now."},{"id":"CP1-03","week":1,"target":"Main: background","prompt":"The sun ___ (shine) when we left the hotel.","options":[],"key":"was shining","reason":"Background to the main event."},{"id":"CP1-04","week":1,"target":"Main: sequence","prompt":"When I opened the fridge, I realised someone ___ (eat) my cake.","options":[],"key":"had eaten","reason":"It happened before I opened the fridge."},{"id":"CP1-05","week":1,"target":"Light","prompt":"As a teenager, I ___ have very long hair.","options":["used to","would"],"key":"used to","reason":"''Have'' (possession) is a state, so would is not possible."},{"id":"CP1-06","week":2,"target":"Main: intention","prompt":"A: Any plans for the summer? B: I ___ visit my cousins in Ireland, but I haven''t booked anything yet.","options":["''m going to","''m visiting"],"key":"''m going to","reason":"An intention with nothing arranged yet."},{"id":"CP1-07","week":2,"target":"Main: arrangement","prompt":"We ___ (fly) to Lisbon on Friday. The tickets are in my bag.","options":[],"key":"''re flying (are flying)","reason":"A fixed arrangement."},{"id":"CP1-08","week":2,"target":"Main: time clause","prompt":"I''ll send you the photos when I ___ home.","options":["get","''ll get"],"key":"get","reason":"After ''when'', use the present simple for the future."},{"id":"CP1-09","week":2,"target":"Main: time clause","prompt":"As soon as the film ___ (finish), we''ll go for dinner.","options":[],"key":"finishes","reason":"After ''as soon as'', use the present simple for the future."},{"id":"CP1-10","week":2,"target":"Light","prompt":"If I ___ the lottery, I''d buy a house by the sea.","options":["won","win"],"key":"won","reason":"Second conditional: an imagined situation."},{"id":"CP1-11","week":3,"target":"Main: obligation","prompt":"In the UK, you ___ drive on the left.","options":["have to","don''t have to"],"key":"have to","reason":"It is a rule."},{"id":"CP1-12","week":3,"target":"Main: advice","prompt":"If you want to improve your English, you ___ read a little every day.","options":["should","mustn''t"],"key":"should","reason":"Advice."},{"id":"CP1-13","week":3,"target":"Main: ability","prompt":"My grandmother ___ (can / not / use) a smartphone, so we phone her.","options":[],"key":"can''t use (cannot use)","reason":"Ability, negative."},{"id":"CP1-14","week":3,"target":"Main: permission","prompt":"___ I leave my bag here while I go to the toilet?","options":["Can","Must"],"key":"Can (Could)","reason":"Asking for permission."},{"id":"CP1-15","week":3,"target":"Light","prompt":"Put the words in order: Where / you / do / work?","options":[],"key":"Where do you work?","reason":"Auxiliary before the subject."},{"id":"CP1-16","week":4,"target":"Main: present passive","prompt":"Cheese ___ (make) from milk.","options":[],"key":"is made","reason":"A general fact; the cheese is the focus."},{"id":"CP1-17","week":4,"target":"Main: present passive","prompt":"Most of the city''s buses ___ by electricity now.","options":["are powered","power"],"key":"are powered","reason":"Something powers the buses."},{"id":"CP1-18","week":4,"target":"Main: past passive","prompt":"The first email ___ (send) in 1971.","options":[],"key":"was sent","reason":"Past passive."},{"id":"CP1-19","week":4,"target":"Main: past passive","prompt":"Our flight ___ because of the snow.","options":["was cancelled","cancelled"],"key":"was cancelled","reason":"The airline cancelled it."},{"id":"CP1-20","week":4,"target":"Light","prompt":"This is the hotel ___ we stayed last summer.","options":["where","who"],"key":"where","reason":"''Where'' for a place followed by a full clause."}],"reserves":[{"id":"CP1-R1","week":1,"target":"reserve","prompt":"I ___ (not / see) her since the wedding.","options":[],"key":"haven''t seen (have not seen)","reason":"Up to now with since."},{"id":"CP1-R2","week":2,"target":"reserve","prompt":"Don''t worry, I ___ (call) you before I ___ (leave).","options":[],"key":"''ll call ... leave","reason":"Will for the promise; present simple after before."},{"id":"CP1-R3","week":3,"target":"reserve","prompt":"You ___ (not / have to) come to the party if you''re tired.","options":[],"key":"don''t have to","reason":"It isn''t necessary."},{"id":"CP1-R4","week":4,"target":"reserve","prompt":"The Alhambra ___ (visit) by millions of people every year.","options":[],"key":"is visited","reason":"Present passive with by."}],"reserveUse":"Reserves replace an item that pilot data shows is unclear, or form a retake for learners repeating the checkpoint.","speakingTask":"A recorded 60–90 second narrative in response to a new prompt about a change, from the weeks 1–4 speaking content.","writing":{"prompts":[{"label":"A. A change I got used to","text":"Describe how life was before a change, what happened, what was difficult, and how things are now."},{"label":"B. A note for a visitor","text":"A friend is visiting your town for a weekend. Recommend what to see: include a regular event or custom, one fact about a place''s past, a comparison, and one piece of advice."}],"conditions":[{"id":"length","setting":"Length","value":"150 words (130–170 accepted)"},{"id":"time","setting":"Time","value":"30 minutes, with a visible timer"},{"id":"where","setting":"Where","value":"In the app; pasting disabled; no phrase bank or model"},{"id":"attempts","setting":"Attempts","value":"One submission; no revise-and-retry"},{"id":"marking","setting":"Marking","value":"AI bands on the four writing criteria straight away; a teacher confirms where one is involved, and the teacher''s mark counts"}]},"result":{"intro":"Results are reported by part and by week, never as pass or fail. Learners continue to week 5 whatever their result; the checkpoint guides practice, it does not block progress.","thresholds":[{"part":"Quiz","onTarget":"14 of 20 or more (70%)"},{"part":"Speaking","onTarget":"''On target'' or better on at least three criteria, and task achievement not at ''Getting there''"},{"part":"Writing","onTarget":"''On target'' or better on at least three criteria, and task achievement not at ''Getting there''"}],"practiceLinks":"Each part below target links to the matching practice: weak quiz items to that week''s extra items and grammar clinic, speaking to the week''s shadowing and conversation, writing to a revise-and-retry task on the same prompt."},"calibration":["A second teacher checks every checkpoint item for a single correct answer and accepted variants.","Check the existing 24 placement questions against the blueprint (6 A2, 8 B1, 6 B1+, 4 B2) and replace those that do not fit.","Mark 10–20 sample texts and recordings by hand and compare with the AI''s bands; adjust prompts until they agree on at least 8 in 10.","After 30 placed learners, compare placement with EF SET results and adjust the cut scores (11/12 and 18/19).","Review any checkpoint item that more than 90% or fewer than 30% of pilot learners answer correctly.","Confirm the checkpoint thresholds (70% quiz, three of four criteria) against teacher judgement of pilot learners."]}}'::jsonb->'checkpoint1')
on conflict (code) do update set title = excluded.title, payload = excluded.payload;

insert into public.syllabus_vocab_items (id, week_number, group_kind, target, cefr, use_role, example, card, sort_order)
select v.id, v.week_number, v.group_kind, v.target, v.cefr, v.use_role, v.example, v.card, v.sort_order
from jsonb_to_recordset('[{"id":"W1-CO-1","week_number":1,"group_kind":"core","target":"adapt","cefr":"B2","use_role":"B","example":"I had to adapt to living abroad.","card":"New","sort_order":1},{"id":"W1-CO-2","week_number":1,"group_kind":"core","target":"turning point","cefr":"B2*","use_role":"B","example":"Moving to Leeds was a turning point in my life.","card":"New","sort_order":2},{"id":"W1-CO-3","week_number":1,"group_kind":"core","target":"challenge","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"I faced several challenges while I was studying abroad.","card":"New","sort_order":3},{"id":"W1-CO-4","week_number":1,"group_kind":"core","target":"get used to","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"It took me a month to get used to living alone.","card":"New","sort_order":4},{"id":"W1-CO-5","week_number":1,"group_kind":"core","target":"look back on","cefr":"B2*","use_role":"B","example":"When I look back on my first year abroad, I remember the people I met.","card":"New","sort_order":5},{"id":"W1-CO-6","week_number":1,"group_kind":"core","target":"regret","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"I''ve never regretted leaving my old job.","card":"New","sort_order":6},{"id":"W1-CO-7","week_number":1,"group_kind":"core","target":"gradually","cefr":"B2*","use_role":"B","example":"My English gradually improved while I was living in York.","card":"New","sort_order":7},{"id":"W1-CO-8","week_number":1,"group_kind":"core","target":"memorable","cefr":"B2*","use_role":"B","example":"Travelling alone was a memorable experience.","card":"New","sort_order":8},{"id":"W1-CO-9","week_number":1,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"make a big decision","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"I made a big decision about my future.","card":"New","sort_order":9},{"id":"W1-CO-10","week_number":1,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"take a risk","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"I took a risk and applied for a job abroad.","card":"New","sort_order":10},{"id":"W1-CO-11","week_number":1,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"make a change","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"I decided to make a change and cycle to work.","card":"New","sort_order":11},{"id":"W1-CO-12","week_number":1,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"keep in touch","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"I''ve kept in touch with my old school friends.","card":"New","sort_order":12},{"id":"W1-CO-13","week_number":1,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"make progress","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"I''ve been making good progress since September.","card":"New","sort_order":13},{"id":"W1-CO-14","week_number":1,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"take up","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"I took up photography after I moved.","card":"New","sort_order":14},{"id":"W1-FA-15","week_number":1,"group_kind":"family","target":"make a big decision","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"decision, decisive, indecisive","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":15},{"id":"W1-FA-16","week_number":1,"group_kind":"family","target":"adapt","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"adaptable","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":16},{"id":"W1-FA-17","week_number":1,"group_kind":"family","target":"make a change","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"unchanged","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":17},{"id":"W1-LI-18","week_number":1,"group_kind":"linker","target":"eventually","cefr":"B2","use_role":null,"example":"Eventually, I got used to it. (time, writing task)","card":"New","sort_order":18},{"id":"W1-LI-19","week_number":1,"group_kind":"linker","target":"since then","cefr":"B1*","use_role":null,"example":"I moved in September. Since then, I''ve made some good friends. (time, writing task)","card":"New","sort_order":19},{"id":"W2-CO-1","week_number":2,"group_kind":"core","target":"ambition","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"Her ambition is to run her own restaurant.","card":"New","sort_order":1},{"id":"W2-CO-2","week_number":2,"group_kind":"core","target":"goal","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"My goal is to start a career in design.","card":"New","sort_order":2},{"id":"W2-CO-3","week_number":2,"group_kind":"core","target":"achieve","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"If you practise regularly, you''ll achieve your goal.","card":"New","sort_order":3},{"id":"W2-CO-4","week_number":2,"group_kind":"core","target":"intend","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"We intend to move to the coast next year.","card":"New","sort_order":4},{"id":"W2-CO-5","week_number":2,"group_kind":"core","target":"career","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"She''s going to start a career in engineering.","card":"New","sort_order":5},{"id":"W2-CO-6","week_number":2,"group_kind":"core","target":"deadline","cefr":"B2","use_role":"B","example":"The deadline for applications is 30 April.","card":"New","sort_order":6},{"id":"W2-CO-7","week_number":2,"group_kind":"core","target":"apply","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"She''s going to apply for a job at the museum.","card":"New","sort_order":7},{"id":"W2-CO-8","week_number":2,"group_kind":"core","target":"look forward to","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"I''m looking forward to starting my new course.","card":"New","sort_order":8},{"id":"W2-CO-9","week_number":2,"group_kind":"core","target":"determined","cefr":"B1","use_role":"B","example":"He''s determined to pass, so he''s going to practise every day.","card":"New","sort_order":9},{"id":"W2-CO-10","week_number":2,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"work towards","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"I''m working towards a degree in nursing.","card":"New","sort_order":10},{"id":"W2-CO-11","week_number":2,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"take the first step","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"I''ll take the first step and contact the college.","card":"New","sort_order":11},{"id":"W2-CO-12","week_number":2,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"improve your skills","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"This course will help you improve your skills.","card":"New","sort_order":12},{"id":"W2-CO-13","week_number":2,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"put (something) off","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"Don''t put off booking the course. With a pronoun: put it off.","card":"New","sort_order":13},{"id":"W2-CO-14","week_number":2,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"set a goal","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"I''m going to set myself a goal of reading one book a month.","card":"New","sort_order":14},{"id":"W2-CO-15","week_number":2,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"meet a deadline","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"We''ll need to finish on Thursday to meet Friday''s deadline.","card":"New","sort_order":15},{"id":"W2-FA-16","week_number":2,"group_kind":"family","target":"ambition","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"ambitious","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":16},{"id":"W2-FA-17","week_number":2,"group_kind":"family","target":"achieve","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"achievement, achievable","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":17},{"id":"W2-FA-18","week_number":2,"group_kind":"family","target":"success","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"succeed, success, successful, successfully","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":18},{"id":"W2-LI-19","week_number":2,"group_kind":"linker","target":"in order to","cefr":"B1","use_role":null,"example":"In order to save money, I''ll cook at home. (purpose, writing task)","card":"New","sort_order":19},{"id":"W3-CO-1","week_number":3,"group_kind":"core","target":"get on with","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"You don''t have to be close friends to get on with your colleagues.","card":"New","sort_order":1},{"id":"W3-CO-2","week_number":3,"group_kind":"core","target":"catch up (with)","cefr":"B2","use_role":"B","example":"Can we meet after work and catch up? Here: exchange news.","card":"New","sort_order":2},{"id":"W3-CO-3","week_number":3,"group_kind":"core","target":"arrange","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"We should arrange to meet outside the station.","card":"New","sort_order":3},{"id":"W3-CO-4","week_number":3,"group_kind":"core","target":"routine","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"Try to stick to a routine during busy weeks.","card":"New","sort_order":4},{"id":"W3-CO-5","week_number":3,"group_kind":"core","target":"rely on","cefr":"B2","use_role":"B","example":"You can rely on Maria to help if there''s a problem.","card":"New","sort_order":5},{"id":"W3-CO-6","week_number":3,"group_kind":"core","target":"misunderstanding","cefr":"B2","use_role":"B","example":"We should talk and clear up the misunderstanding.","card":"New","sort_order":6},{"id":"W3-CO-7","week_number":3,"group_kind":"core","target":"invite (someone) round","cefr":"B1*","use_role":"P","example":"Can I invite some friends round on Saturday? BrE.","card":"New","sort_order":7},{"id":"W3-CO-8","week_number":3,"group_kind":"core","target":"awkward (situation)","cefr":"B2","use_role":"B","example":"It was an awkward situation, but we managed to talk it through.","card":"New","sort_order":8},{"id":"W3-CO-9","week_number":3,"group_kind":"core","target":"politely","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"You can disagree politely.","card":"New","sort_order":9},{"id":"W3-CO-10","week_number":3,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"make an effort","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"We should make an effort to welcome new colleagues.","card":"New","sort_order":10},{"id":"W3-CO-11","week_number":3,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"have a lot in common","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"We have a lot in common: we both love cycling.","card":"New","sort_order":11},{"id":"W3-CO-12","week_number":3,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"get in touch","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"You should get in touch with the organiser.","card":"New","sort_order":12},{"id":"W3-CO-13","week_number":3,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"come over","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"Can you come over for coffee on Saturday?","card":"New","sort_order":13},{"id":"W3-CO-14","week_number":3,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"keep a promise","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"You should keep a promise even if it''s difficult.","card":"New","sort_order":14},{"id":"W3-FA-15","week_number":3,"group_kind":"family","target":"friend","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"unfriendly, friendship","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":15},{"id":"W3-FA-16","week_number":3,"group_kind":"family","target":"politely","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"politeness, impolite","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":16},{"id":"W3-FA-17","week_number":3,"group_kind":"family","target":"rely on","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"reliable, unreliable, reliably","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":17},{"id":"W3-OP-18","week_number":3,"group_kind":"optional","target":"pop round","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"Can I pop round after work? Informal BrE; short visit.","card":"Recognition only","sort_order":18},{"id":"W3-LI-19","week_number":3,"group_kind":"linker","target":"on the other hand","cefr":"B1","use_role":null,"example":"Living with friends can be fun. On the other hand, you have to share the housework. (contrast, grammar task)","card":"New","sort_order":19},{"id":"W3-LI-20","week_number":3,"group_kind":"linker","target":"in fact","cefr":"B1","use_role":null,"example":"We get on really well. In fact, we talk almost every day. (emphasis, grammar task)","card":"New","sort_order":20},{"id":"W3-LI-21","week_number":3,"group_kind":"linker","target":"apart from that","cefr":"B1*","use_role":null,"example":"The bus was late. Apart from that, the day went well. (exception, grammar task)","card":"New","sort_order":21},{"id":"W4-CO-1","week_number":4,"group_kind":"core","target":"tradition","cefr":"B2","use_role":"B","example":"Visitors are invited to take part in a local tradition.","card":"New","sort_order":1},{"id":"W4-CO-2","week_number":4,"group_kind":"core","target":"custom","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"The guide explained a local custom: visitors are asked to take off their shoes before they go inside.","card":"New","sort_order":2},{"id":"W4-CO-3","week_number":4,"group_kind":"core","target":"destination","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"It''s one of the most popular holiday destinations on the coast.","card":"New","sort_order":3},{"id":"W4-CO-4","week_number":4,"group_kind":"core","target":"set off","cefr":"B2","use_role":"B","example":"We set off early to avoid the heavy traffic.","card":"New","sort_order":4},{"id":"W4-CO-5","week_number":4,"group_kind":"core","target":"get around","cefr":"B1*","use_role":"P","example":"We were given a map to help us get around the city.","card":"New","sort_order":5},{"id":"W4-CO-6","week_number":4,"group_kind":"core","target":"unfamiliar","cefr":"B2","use_role":"B","example":"We were unfamiliar with the ticket system.","card":"New","sort_order":6},{"id":"W4-CO-7","week_number":4,"group_kind":"core","target":"welcoming","cefr":"B2*","use_role":"B","example":"The hotel where we stayed had a welcoming atmosphere.","card":"New","sort_order":7},{"id":"W4-CO-8","week_number":4,"group_kind":"core","target":"local","cefr":"B1","use_role":"P","example":"Local food is served in the hotel restaurant.","card":"New","sort_order":8},{"id":"W4-CO-9","week_number":4,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"take a guided tour","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"We took a guided tour of the old town.","card":"New","sort_order":9},{"id":"W4-CO-10","week_number":4,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"try the local food","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"We were encouraged to try the local food.","card":"New","sort_order":10},{"id":"W4-CO-11","week_number":4,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"travel light","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"We travelled light because there wasn''t much room for luggage.","card":"New","sort_order":11},{"id":"W4-CO-12","week_number":4,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"stop overnight","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"We stopped overnight in York before driving on.","card":"New","sort_order":12},{"id":"W4-CO-13","week_number":4,"group_kind":"collocation","target":"miss a connection","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"Our flight was delayed, so we missed our connection.","card":"New","sort_order":13},{"id":"W4-FA-14","week_number":4,"group_kind":"family","target":"culture","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"culture, cultural, culturally","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":14},{"id":"W4-FA-15","week_number":4,"group_kind":"family","target":"tradition","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"traditional, traditionally","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":15},{"id":"W4-FA-16","week_number":4,"group_kind":"family","target":"tourism","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"tourism, touristy","card":"Shared / recognition","sort_order":16},{"id":"W4-OP-17","week_number":4,"group_kind":"optional","target":"break your journey","cefr":null,"use_role":null,"example":"We broke our journey with an overnight stay in York. Mainly BrE.","card":"Recognition only","sort_order":17},{"id":"W4-LI-18","week_number":4,"group_kind":"linker","target":"to begin with","cefr":"B1","use_role":null,"example":"To begin with, we were shown around the old town. (sequence, writing task)","card":"New","sort_order":18},{"id":"W4-LI-19","week_number":4,"group_kind":"linker","target":"what''s more","cefr":"B2","use_role":null,"example":"The hotel was comfortable. What''s more, breakfast was included. (addition, writing task)","card":"New","sort_order":19},{"id":"W4-LI-20","week_number":4,"group_kind":"linker","target":"despite","cefr":"B1","use_role":null,"example":"Despite the rain, the outdoor tour went ahead. (concession, writing task)","card":"New","sort_order":20},{"id":"W4-LI-21","week_number":4,"group_kind":"linker","target":"all in all","cefr":"B2*","use_role":null,"example":"All in all, we had an excellent trip. (summary, writing task)","card":"New","sort_order":21}]'::jsonb) as v(
